• A polynomial p ∈ P(F) is said to have degree m if there exist scalars a0, a1, ..., am ∈ F with am ≠ 0 such that for every z ∈ F, we have
p(z) = a0 + a1z + ⋯ + amzm.
• The polynomial that is identically 0 is said to have degree −∞.
