Proof Because T is a linear map, T(0) = 0 (by 3.10). Thus 0 ∈ null T. Suppose u, v ∈ null T. Then
T(u + v) = Tu + Tv = 0 + 0 = 0.
Hence u + v ∈ null T. Thus null T is closed under addition. Suppose u ∈ null T and λ ∈ F. Then
