Suppose T ∈ L(R3) is defined by T(x, y, z) = (−y, x, 4z). Thus T is a counterclockwise rotation by 90∘ in the xy-plane and a stretch by a factor of 4 in the direction of the z-axis. Hence the inverse map T−1 ∈ L(R3) is the clockwise rotation by 90∘ in the xy-plane and a stretch by a factor of 1
4 in the direction of the z-axis:
T−1(x, y, z) = (y, −x, 1
4 z).
